<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Musta'li</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1074">1074</a>–1101</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Musta'li (1074–1101) was the ninth Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, ruling from 1094 to 1101. A younger son of al-Mustansir, he was placed on the throne by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-afdal">al-Afdal</a> in preference to his elder brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismailism">Nizar</a>, splitting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> movement into Musta'li and Nizari branches. During his reign the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a> reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, and the crusaders took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> in 1099.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-mustali.jpg" alt="Al-Musta'li" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, 11th/12th-century mint master · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_dinar_of_al-Musta%27li_billah,_AH_493.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
